    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.00 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00204 is refunded in full to the rider. No compensation is payable to the driver.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. The driver accepted at 12:33:20 and the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50. The GPS trace (100% coverage, 87 fixes, max gap 0.0 s) places him inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 12:41:50 to 12:47:30 — a single continuous hold of 340 seconds, 40 seconds beyond the 300-second minimum (derived shortfall -40.0 s) — and he cancelled at 12:47:30 on RIDER_UNREACHABLE with no boarding event. On the arrival-and-dwell side the driver's POL-NS-01 case is made out, and the rider advocate correctly conceded it.\n\nWHY THE DRIVER NONETHELESS DOES NOT KEEP THE FEE. POL-NS-01 stands only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does. That clause refunds the fee in full, with no driver compensation, where (a) the rider sent a locating or coordinating message in the waiting window, (b) the driver neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call before terminating, and (c) the rider's device was inside the presence radius for the majority of qualifying fixes. All three hold. (a) The rider messaged at 12:44:40 — 'boss? i still cannot see u leh' — inside the window, and had earlier written at 12:41:05 'im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?'. (b) The chat log contains no driver message at any point and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty; both rider messages were delivered and read (12:41:22 and 12:44:52) and the 120-second window expired twice over before the 12:47:30 cancellation. (c) The rider track holds 105 fixes, every one qualifying, never more than 39.94 m from the pin (mean 21.08 m) — far inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE radius — for the whole waiting window.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CLAIMS. His claim that all four POL-NS-01 conditions are met is accepted, but that clause asks only whether POL-NS-01 is displaced, and POL-NS-04 displaces it; the fee does not turn on dwell alone. His claim that there is no shortfall under POL-NS-06 is accepted (effective dwell 340 s against a 300 s minimum), but POL-NS-06 is not the deciding clause here. His claim that the arrival marker is genuine and not a false arrival under POL-NS-05 is accepted (minimum approach 94.94 m, well inside the 300 m threshold, and no in-motion marker), and no false-arrival referral arises under POL-NS-05(ii) because qualifying in-geofence fixes exist. His claim that the artifacts are complete at weight 1.0 and that no profile escalation trips is accepted. His claim to POL-NS-07 compensation fails: compensation is payable only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 displaces it. (The anti-farming check would not trip in any event: no_show_terminations_30d 3 is below 4, and 3/142 = 0.021 is below 0.08.) One factual point in his contact claim is not accepted: the rider did state her sub-location — 'entrance 3 phv pickup point', matching the recorded pickup point — so the suggestion that she named no bay or entrance is not borne out by MSG-00204-001.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CLAIMS. Her claims that POL-NS-04 limbs (a), (b) and (c) hold are accepted, and her claim that this is not a wrong-entrance or pin-ambiguity case under POL-NS-03 is accepted: the driver's own fixes place him inside the arrival radius, so the 400 m ceiling is never reached and no pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii) arises.\n\nEVIDENCE INTEGRITY AND CONFIDENCE. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace, the trip record and the chat log — is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, with no clock skew (POL-NS-08(a)), no trace gap (b), no chat truncation (c) and no fare mismatch (d: $4.00 = greater of the $4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the $4.00 RYDE_X tier fee), so POL-NS-08 is not engaged. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00204-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is cited only for its absence, carries no fact, and is not needed: POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable and the single 340-second hold already exceeds the minimum. No profile field drives this outcome; only the trailing-window counters the clauses name were read, and the driver's lifetime prior_no_show_flags of 1 was not used as a ground. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other, no same-party repeat disputes, no anti-farming trip), so the refund issues now rather than the fee being held. The refund is $4.00 of the $4.50 charged; the remaining $0.50 is the platform fee, which is not in dispute."
